hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"61","[AI-translation] Abd-ur-Rahman, aur woh Ibn-e-Yazid As-San'ani, kehte hain ke maine Ibn-e-Umar ko kehte hue suna ke Rasoolullah (sallallahu alayhi wa sallam) ne farmaya: Jis shakhs ko yeh khushi ho ke woh qayamat ke din ko aankhon ke dekhe jaisa dekh le toh woh padhe ""Izash-shamsu kuwwirat"" aur ""Izash-sama-unfatirat"" aur ""Izash-sama-anshaqqat"". Yeh hadith hasan gharib hai. Aur Hisham ibn-e-Yusuf aur doosron ne is hadith ko isi isnaad ke saath rivayat kiya hai aur farmaya: Jis shakhs ko yeh khushi ho ke woh qayamat ke din ko aankhon ke dekhe jaisa dekh le toh woh padhe ""Izash-shamsu kuwwirat"", aur unhone ""Izash-sama-unfatirat"" aur ""Izash-sama-anshaqqat"" ka zikr nahi kiya."
"62","[AI-translation] Ubayy ibn-e-Ka'b kehte hain ke Rasoolullah (sallallahu alayhi wa sallam) witr ki pehli rak'at mein ""Sabbih-isma-rabbikal-a'la"", dusri mein ""Qul yaa ayyuhal-kafiroon"" aur teesri mein ""Qul huwal-lahu ahad"" padhte the."
"63","[AI-translation] Samrah ibn-e-Jundub se riwayat hai ke Rasoolullah (sallallahu alayhi wa sallam) jumah ki namaz mein ""Sabbih-isma-rabbikal-a'la"" aur ""Hal ataka hadith-ul-ghashiya"" padhte the."
